.TH CLAUDE-ACCOUNT 1 "November 14, 2026" "dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude-account \- run Claude Code with isolated account profiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-account auth-login
.I profile
.RB [ --replace ]
.br
.B claude-account
.I profile
.RI [ "claude arguments..." ]
.br
.B claude-account default
.RI [ profile | --clear ]
.br
.B claude-account repair
.I profile
.br
.B claude-account list
.br
.B claude-account ps
.RI [ profile ]
.br
.B claude-account kill
.IR "profile | --all"
.B --force
.br
.B claude-account
.RB "help | --help | -h | man"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each profile uses its own CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and regular OAuth login.
Claude Code 2.1.261 or later is required for account operations.
Other profiles may remain active during login.
Local transcripts are shared for explicit resume across profiles.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "auth-login " profile " [--replace]"
Log in and register the account identity. Replacing an identity requires
--replace and an interactive confirmation. Active sessions block login,
even with --replace.
.TP
.I "profile [claude arguments...]"
Run Claude with the selected account and forward its arguments.
.TP
.BI "default " "[profile | --clear]"
Show, select or clear the default for future shell launches.
Existing sessions do not change accounts.
.TP
.BI "repair " profile
Repair onboarding state after verifying the registered identity.
.TP
.B list
List registered login profiles.
.TP
.BI "ps " [profile]
List current-user processes attached to profile login locks
and their descendants.
Without a profile, list all managed profiles.
Columns are profile, PID, parent PID,
terminal, role and executable name. Arguments and credentials are not printed.
.TP
.BI "kill " "profile | --all" " --force"
Send SIGKILL to the discovered processes, descendants first.
A profile or explicit --all and --force are required.
This interrupts running work without cleanup and may lose unsaved work.
Prefer /exit for normal shutdown. Run this command from a separate terminal,
not from inside a targeted session.
.TP
.B "help, --help, -h"
Show usage. ps and kill also accept --help or -h.
.TP
.B man
Open this manual directly from the repository.
.SH PROCESS SCOPE
Process commands require python3, ps and lsof.
They identify current-user processes by open full-login.lock files and
the complete claude-account launcher signature. File readers are excluded.
Native Claude launches outside claude-account are excluded.
Detached processes that no longer descend from a lock holder
are excluded. Discovery is a snapshot; processes launched afterwards may
require another invocation. Inspect ps again before retrying login.
Lock files are never deleted. A leftover file without a live holder does
not block login.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
claude-account ps elyza
claude-account kill elyza --force
claude-account auth-login elyza --replace
claude-account ps
claude-account kill --all --force
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Absolute configuration root; defaults to $HOME/.config.
Profiles live under claude-account/accounts/PROFILE.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success, including no matching processes.
Nonzero indicates an invalid argument, discovery error or signal failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR kill (1),
.BR lsof (8)
